here only to identify the hardware that Osprey interoperates with.

The UniFi camera wire protocol implemented in pyunifiwire/ was documented by
observing traffic between devices that the authors own, for the sole purpose
of interoperability. No Ubiquiti firmware, software or other copyrighted
material is distributed with Osprey. Protocol behaviour can change with any
camera firmware update; use Osprey at your own risk, and only with cameras you
own or are authorised to manage.

Osprey does not bundle Frigate, FFmpeg, OpenSSL or Python. Container images
built from docker/Dockerfile include Debian packages (including FFmpeg and
OpenSSL) and paho-mqtt under their own licenses; the image SBOM published with
each release lists them.
